TITLE='Authentic title "30 Unsexy Habits That Make Serious Money ($100,000+)" is a numbered-list frame with a money-outcome promise. The script delivers exactly 30 habits; most come with a compounding figure above $100,000, so the parenthetical is met.'
THUMB='Registered maxresdefault 1280x720 (HTTP 200, real image). White background: the recurring cartoon man in a white shirt with a bored expression in front of a large pile of cash, a black arrow pointing to him, and "BORING = RICH" in heavy black capitals. At 320x180 the words and image read clearly. Matches the script\'s thesis (unglamorous habits build wealth) without naming a number.'
SCRIPT='A single-narrator 52-minute numbered-list essay: a kitchen-table hook, the extraction-economy framing, Ramsey and Stanley millionaire research, then 30 habits grouped as big structures (cars, housing, geography, index funds, HSA, match, automation, cards, debt), daily leaks (emergency fund, food, phone, bulk, impulse rule, library, warranties, subscriptions) and income/negotiation habits (lifestyle creep, tracking, salary, insurance, bills, toys, medical bills, taxes, skills, waiting rule), a Housel quotation, a not-too-late message and a 401(k)-match call to action. Most compounding arithmetic reproduces; Direct File advice is out of date, the HSA investing share is understated, and several survey figures are dated or unsourced.'
